[CENTER][SIZE=6][B]Expressive Launcher 5.2.1 QA (Build 84) — System Accent & ExpressiveOS Palette Fix[/B][/SIZE]
[SIZE=4][I]Official Release Announcement & Download Links[/I][/SIZE][/CENTER]

[HR][/HR]

5.2.1 fixes a [ICODE]5.2.0[/ICODE] regression where setting [B]Accent color[/B] to [B]System[/B] on Android 12+ / ExpressiveOS ignored the system color seed and rendered a hardcoded mint-green/burgundy palette across the App Drawer, themed icons, search bar, and Settings.

[HR][/HR]

[SIZE=5][B]✨ What's New & Improved[/B][/SIZE]

[SIZE=5][B]1. 🎨 Restore System Accent & ExpressiveOS Monet Palette Tracking ([ICODE]5.2.0[/ICODE] regression)[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Before[/B]: [ICODE]5.2.0[/ICODE] switched the [ICODE]expressive[/ICODE] flavor's default [ICODE]color_style[/ICODE] to [ICODE]expressive[/ICODE], exposing a latent cache-key mismatch in [ICODE]ThemeProvider[/ICODE] where [ICODE]SystemColorScheme[/ICODE] was only stored at [ICODE]Pair(0, Style.TONAL_SPOT)[/ICODE]. On Android 12+ with [ICODE]Accent color = System[/ICODE], [ICODE]getColorScheme(0, Style.EXPRESSIVE)[/ICODE] missed the cache and constructed [ICODE]MonetColorSchemeCompat(0, Style.EXPRESSIVE)[/ICODE], where [ICODE]0[/ICODE] ([ICODE]Color.TRANSPARENT[/ICODE]) fell back to hardcoded [ICODE]GOOGLE_BLUE[/ICODE] ([ICODE]#1B6EF3[/ICODE]) rotated by [ICODE]Style.EXPRESSIVE[/ICODE]—causing mint-green accents and burgundy themed-icon circles instead of the OS/eOS system palette.
[*][B]Now[/B]: [ICODE]ThemeProvider[/ICODE] caches [ICODE]SystemColorScheme(context)[/ICODE] in a dedicated [ICODE]systemOverlayColorScheme[/ICODE] field on Android 12+ ([ICODE]Utilities.ATLEAST_S[/ICODE]) and returns it for [ICODE]ColorOption.SystemAccent[/ICODE] regardless of [ICODE]colorStyle[/ICODE], so App Drawer, themed icons, search bar, widgets, and Settings match the system/eOS palette directly.

[/LIST]
[SIZE=5][B]2. 🔄 Live System Overlay Refresh & Non-System Color Style Preservation[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Before[/B]: [ICODE]overlayChangedReceiver[/ICODE] only refreshed [ICODE]colorSchemeMap[Pair(0, Style.TONAL_SPOT)][/ICODE], so system theme/wallpaper changes never invalidated non-[ICODE]TONAL_SPOT[/ICODE] entries, and users who previously tried a custom color style and returned to [B]System[/B] remained stuck on the broken fallback.
[*][B]Now[/B]: [ICODE]android.intent.action.OVERLAY_CHANGED[/ICODE] (for [ICODE]package:android[/ICODE]) always refreshes [ICODE]systemOverlayColorScheme[/ICODE] and notifies listeners; [B]Custom[/B] and [B]Wallpaper[/B] accent modes continue to default to M3 Expressive ([ICODE]Style.EXPRESSIVE[/ICODE]) and respect user-selected color styles.

[/LIST]
[SIZE=5][B]3. ✅ OTA Cleanup Race Fix, Regression Coverage & GitHub Issue Closure[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]Fixed a race in [ICODE]NightlyBuildsRepository.installUpdate()[/ICODE] so invalid downloaded APKs are deleted before emitting [ICODE]UpdateState.Failed[/ICODE].
[*]Added [ICODE]ThemeProviderSystemPaletteTest[/ICODE] covering real [ICODE]ThemeProvider[/ICODE] resolution (no [ICODE]ShadowThemeProvider[/ICODE]) across SDK 36 and SDK 37 for default [ICODE]SystemAccent[/ICODE] + [ICODE]Expressive[/ICODE], all [ICODE]ColorStyle[/ICODE] values, [ICODE]OVERLAY_CHANGED[/ICODE] refresh, and [ICODE]CustomColor[/ICODE] → [ICODE]SystemAccent[/ICODE] switching.
[*]Audited and closed shipped GitHub feature requests [ICODE]#73[/ICODE] (custom icons from images) and [ICODE]#74[/ICODE] (hide app badge on shortcuts), both shipped since [ICODE]5.1.7 (80)[/ICODE].

[/LIST]
[HR][/HR]

